# Project Name: koshiv - Learning App for Kids
# Role: Docker Engineer
# Original File Version: 1.0.0.0.0
# Complete Version Tracing:
# Version 1.0.0.0.0 | Initial .gitignore creation — excluding sensitive .env files, OS artifacts, and IDE configs
# Version 1.0.0.0.1 | Added JWT keys exclusion — private.pem and public.pem must never be committed
#
# Aim: Git Ignore Rules
# Why: Prevents accidental exposure of sensitive credentials (.env),
#      operating system generated files (Thumbs.db, .DS_Store), and
#      IDE-specific configurations (.vscode/, .idea/) from being committed
#      to version control. The .env file contains real database passwords
#      and Tailscale IP — its exclusion is a security requirement per
#      Sovereign Rulebook. .env.example with dummy values will be committed
#      instead for developer reference.

# Sensitive Environment Files (CRITICAL)
.env
*.env
!*.env.example

# OS Generated Files
Thumbs.db
.DS_Store
Desktop.ini

# IDE Configurations
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo

# JWT Keys (CRITICAL - Security)
keys/*.pem